content='<div class="s6-hide"><p>Build a one-objective action plan with a measurable outcome and bounded resources. This manual worksheet is not a full business plan, AI generator or connected dashboard.</p><p><a href="/downloads/strategic-plan-template.pdf" download>Download the two-page blank/example PDF</a></p><noscript><p>Editable controls need JavaScript. The guide and static PDF remain available.</p></noscript><h2>Prepare your plan</h2><form id="s6-form">'+fields+'<h3>Actions (1–20)</h3><div id="s6-rows"></div><button id="s6-add" type="button">Add action</button><button type="submit">Review strategic plan</button><button id="s6-sample" type="button">Load fictional example</button></form><p id="s6-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></div><h2>Your reviewed strategic plan</h2><div id="s6-result" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="s6-hide"><h2>Keep your plan</h2><p>No automatic saving. Reloading or closing loses entries unless you download an editable JSON backup. This worksheet does not transmit entries. Keep sensitive information out of shared copies. Free-tool backups do not import into paid products.</p><button id="s6-backup" type="button">Download JSON backup</button><label>Import same-tool JSON (128 KB maximum)<input id="s6-import" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"></label><button id="s6-export" type="button" disabled>Download reviewed CSV</button><button id="s6-print" type="button" disabled>Print / Save PDF</button><button id="s6-clear" type="button">Clear entries</button><dialog id="s6-import-dialog"><h2>Replace current entries?</h2><p>A valid same-tool backup is ready; import replaces this page.</p><button id="s6-confirm" type="button">Replace entries</button><button id="s6-cancel" type="button">Cancel</button></dialog><dialog id="s6-clear-dialog"><h2>Clear page entries?</h2><p>Downloaded backups remain on your device.</p><button id="s6-clear-confirm" type="button">Clear entries</button><button id="s6-clear-cancel" type="button">Cancel</button></dialog>'
content+=body("""## How to use this strategic-plan template
Choose one objective, accountable owner and fixed plan period. State a metric unit, source, definition and comparable measurement windows. Enter nonnegative whole baseline, target and current values up to one million. Target must differ from baseline. For decimal metrics, choose a consistent smaller whole unit and explain the conversion; do not mix units.
Record 1–20 actions with an owner, due date within the plan period, planned whole minutes from zero to 10,080, allocated USD cost and manual status. Enter the total available minutes and period budget separately. The worksheet sums effort and allocations across all actions, including completed ones; it does not calculate remaining work, recurring costs or day-level conflicts.
## Metric change is not task completion
Metric progress = (current − baseline) ÷ (target − baseline) × 100. A lower target means a decrease is intended; a higher target means an increase. The raw result can be negative or above 100%. It is a change relative to the chosen baseline and target, not a forecast, causal effect or action-completion percentage. Keep the definition and measurement windows consistent.
Actions done ÷ all actions is a separate status percentage. Marking every task done does not prove the outcome metric improved. A target equal to baseline is rejected because the progress formula would have a zero denominator. No progress percentage is invented for that case.
## Original fictional example
Baseline 20 qualified inquiries, target 40 and current 30 represent 50.0% of the baseline-to-target increase, with ten units still to target. The example uses two stated matched 30-day windows rather than comparing a partial period with a full month. These are invented observations, not actual customer results.
Three actions allocate 180, 240 and 60 minutes, totaling 480 against 420 available minutes: a 60-minute capacity gap. Allocated costs of $100, $150 and $50 total $300 against a $350 budget: $50 headroom. One of three actions is marked done, or 33.3%, separate from the 50.0% metric change. Resolve the resource gap rather than treating the budget surplus as additional time.
## Save, export and review
JSON restores editable inputs in this same tool after validation and confirmation. CSV exports reviewed plan fields and actions with spreadsheet-formula protection. Every input edit invalidates the previous report and disables CSV/print until reviewed again. Print opens the browser dialog; inspect pagination and PDF options. The separate two-page US Letter PDF contains a blank writing sheet and fictional example; it is static, not fillable.
No reminders, AI advice, bank connection, automatic metric collection, calendar sync or automatic storage are supplied. Dates and statuses are entered by you. Use the [one-page business-plan guide](/journal/one-page-business-plan-template-assumptions/) for wider assumptions and the [weekly time-blocking worksheet](/tools/time-blocking-template/) for actual calendar windows. Use the [business review guide](/journal/business-planner-weekly-review/) for a recurring decision routine.
## Frequently asked questions
Can this replace a complete strategic plan? It is a one-objective working sheet, not a full organizational strategy or lender document. Does budget headroom equal bank cash? No, it is entered budget minus entered allocations. Can a negative progress be valid? Yes: it means the entered current value moved away from the chosen target relative to baseline. Check units and evidence before interpreting it.
""")+'</div>'
